==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 97% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 95% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 93% HP:
**1 [[Gory]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 92% HP:
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Croco]]s spawn , delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 1~10 seconds<sup>30f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
When the battle begins, start upgrading your [[Worker Cat]] to max level. When the enemies get close to your base, send out a few [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cats]]. Don't get scared when Squire Rel appears, as she can easily be killed by the [[Cat Cannon]] or even meatshields. Eventually your money will be maxed out; that's when you can send out all of your [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] at once. When they start to hit the enemy base, start spawning [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cats]] and [[Bird Cat (Normal Cat)|UFO Cats]] to kill all of the Gories. After stopping the enemy frontlines, you will have to deal with Mooth. Luckily, all those dead Gories should've given you a lot of money, which you can use quite wisely by deploying [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Titan Cats]] for an easy win.

